param=dom_arena_type,1
param=dom_boss_victory_alternative,dom_general_khazzard_giant_safe
param=dom_boss_desc,This skeletal Mahjarrat is one of the youngest of his race. He doesn't seem to have a guilty conscience about kidnapping rich people to fight in his arena, so he probably won't worry about fighting dirty.<br><br><col=F5B241>Quest</col>: Fight Arena<br><br><col=F5B241>Combat</col>: He starts off small and ugly, but when you kill his first version you'll be confronted with a larger, deadlier and, quite possibly, uglier version of the Mahjarrat man. He attacks with melee.
param=dom_boss_1_taunt,Taste my vengeance.
param=dom_boss_taunt_sound_english,khazard_taste_my_vengeance
param=dom_boss_taunt_sound_german,khazard_taste_my_vengeance
param=dom_boss_taunt_sound_french,khazard_taste_my_vengeance
param=dom_boss_taunt_sound_portuguese,khazard_taste_my_vengeance
param=dom_battle_total_lifepoints,12000
param=dom_boss_spline_size,0
param=dom_boss_thumbnail,aif_dom_general_khazard

// 2785
[dom_boss_black_knight_guardian]
param=dom_boss_name,The Black Knight Guardian
param=dom_boss_id,30
param=dom_boss_npc_safe_1,dom_black_knight_guardian_safe
param=dom_boss_npc_combat_1,dom_black_knight_guardian_combat
param=dom_npc_spawn_npc1_x,38
param=dom_npc_spawn_npc1_z,32
param=dom_arena_type,3
param=dom_boss_desc,This armour-clad man is an elite guard from the Kinshra (a Zamorakian military order). If it was possible to see his face beneath his mask, a mixture of anger and hatred would be seen.<br><br><col=F5B241>Quest</col>: A Void Dance<br><br><col=F5B241>Combat</col>: The knight attacks with basic melee, but has the special ability of replenishing his life points when his health gets below a certain amount by draining your prayer.
param=dom_boss_1_taunt,Give up! You don't stand a chance!
param=dom_boss_taunt_sound_english,bkg_give_up
param=dom_boss_taunt_sound_german,bkg_give_up
param=dom_boss_taunt_sound_french,bkg_give_up
param=dom_boss_taunt_sound_portuguese,bkg_give_up
param=dom_battle_total_lifepoints,5500
param=dom_boss_spline_size,0
param=dom_boss_thumbnail,aif_dom_black_knight_guardian

// 2786
[dom_boss_dad]
param=dom_boss_name,Dad
param=dom_boss_id,31
param=dom_boss_npc_safe_1,dom_dad_safe
param=dom_boss_npc_combat_1,dom_dad_combat
param=dom_npc_spawn_npc1_x,37
param=dom_npc_spawn_npc1_z,31
param=dom_arena_type,1
param=dom_boss_desc,Like most trolls, Dad was named after his first attempt to eat his own father. Like a giant rock, there's not a great deal of intellect there, but some impressive might. You've been warned.<br><br><col=F5B241>Quest</col>: Troll Stronghold<br><br><col=F5B241>Combat</col>: As well as bashing your brains in with melee combat, Dad has an attack that will hit through pretty much any defence, knocking you back a few paces.
param=dom_boss_1_taunt,Smash the human!
param=dom_boss_taunt_sound_english,dad_smash_the_human
param=dom_boss_taunt_sound_german,dad_smash_the_human
param=dom_boss_taunt_sound_french,dad_smash_the_human
param=dom_boss_taunt_sound_portuguese,dad_smash_the_human
param=dom_battle_total_lifepoints,8000
param=dom_boss_spline_size,0
param=dom_boss_thumbnail,aif_dom_dad

// 2787
[dom_boss_dramen_tree_spirit]
param=dom_boss_name,Dramen Tree Spirit
param=dom_boss_id,32
param=dom_boss_npc_safe_1,dom_dramen_tree_spirit_safe
param=dom_boss_npc_combat_1,dom_dramen_tree_spirit_combat
param=dom_npc_spawn_npc1_x,38
param=dom_npc_spawn_npc1_z,32
param=dom_arena_type,1
param=dom_boss_desc,The guardian of the rare dramen tree, the spirit exists as a guardian to the tree; wood of which is key for any wanting to travel to the plane of Zanaris.<br><br><col=F5B241>Quest</col>: Lost City<br><br><col=F5B241>Combat</col>: Now you can show the spirit how tough you are with more than an axe! (No, you can't hide behind mushrooms to make it easier.)
param=dom_boss_1_taunt,Be away with you mortal
param=dom_boss_taunt_sound_english,dramen_tree_spirit_be_away
param=dom_boss_taunt_sound_german,dramen_tree_spirit_be_away
param=dom_boss_taunt_sound_french,dramen_tree_spirit_be_away
param=dom_boss_taunt_sound_portuguese,dramen_tree_spirit_be_away
param=dom_battle_total_lifepoints,4500
param=dom_boss_spline_size,0
param=dom_boss_thumbnail,aif_dom_dramen_tree_spirit

// 2788
[dom_boss_agrith_naar]
param=dom_boss_name,Agrith Naar
param=dom_boss_id,33
param=dom_boss_npc_safe_1,dom_agrith_naar_safe
param=dom_boss_npc_combat_1,dom_agrith_naar_combat
param=dom_npc_spawn_npc1_x,37
param=dom_npc_spawn_npc1_z,31
param=dom_arena_type,3
param=dom_boss_desc,This big demon came to Gielinor in one of the early ages and is an ancient being with a great wealth of experience in battle.<br><br><col=F5B241>Quest</col>: Shadow of the Storm<br><br><col=F5B241>Combat</col>: Watch out! Agrith Naar will attack with melee and magic, switching depending upon your use of the protection prayers. Agrith Naar will also occasionally teleport you towards him, so attacking from a distance isn't always so easy. You must deal the finishing blow with Silverlight (provided in the arena).
param=dom_boss_1_taunt,Grrrrr
param=dom_boss_taunt_sound_english,greater_demon_attack_4
param=dom_boss_taunt_sound_german,greater_demon_attack_4
param=dom_boss_taunt_sound_french,greater_demon_attack_4
param=dom_boss_taunt_sound_portuguese,greater_demon_attack_4
param=dom_battle_total_lifepoints,6000
param=dom_boss_spline_size,0
param=dom_boss_thumbnail,domtower_icon_agrith_naar

// 2789
[dom_boss_original_dagannoth_mother]
param=dom_boss_name,Dagannoth Mother (version 1)
param=dom_boss_id,34
param=dom_boss_npc_safe_1,dom_original_dagganoth_mother_melee_safe
param=dom_boss_npc_combat_1,dom_original_dagganoth_mother_melee_combat
param=dom_npc_spawn_npc1_x,37
param=dom_npc_spawn_npc1_z,31
param=dom_arena_type,1
param=dom_boss_desc,This is the first dagannoth mother to scare those living in Rellekka; a creature that features predominantly in children's stories among the Fremennik. This nightmare of a sea creature is, unfortunately, very real.<br><br><col=F5B241>Quest</col>: Horror from the Deep<br><br><col=F5B241>Combat</col>: Is anything ever better than the original? Well, this version of the mother changes from one protective type to another in a set order. Remember, to deal damage, consider its colours: blue (water magic); orange (melee attacks); green (ranged attacks); brown (earth magic); red (fire magic); white (air magic). She attacks with melee and ranged, depending on how close and personal you wish to get.<br><br>If you don't have the normal spellbook active, it will become active when you start this battle, and will revert afterwards.
param=dom_boss_1_taunt,Nrraaa
param=dom_boss_taunt_sound_english,dagganoth_mother_changes_4
param=dom_boss_taunt_sound_german,dagganoth_mother_changes_4
param=dom_boss_taunt_sound_french,dagganoth_mother_changes_4
param=dom_boss_taunt_sound_portuguese,dagganoth_mother_changes_4
param=dom_battle_total_lifepoints,9000
param=dom_boss_spline_size,0
param=dom_boss_thumbnail,aif_dom_dagannoth_mother

// 2790
[dom_boss_toktz_ket_dill]
param=dom_boss_name,TokTz-Ket-Dill
param=dom_boss_id,35
param=dom_boss_npc_safe_1,dom_toktz_ket_dill_safe
param=dom_boss_npc_combat_1,dom_toktz_ket_dill_combat
param=dom_npc_spawn_npc1_x,37
param=dom_npc_spawn_npc1_z,31
param=dom_arena_type,1
param=dom_boss_victory_alternative,dom_toktz_ket_dill_cracked_armour_safe
param=dom_boss_desc,This creature has a carapace of obsidian as its initial defence mechanism. In the TzHaar language its name relates to it being an armadillo guarded by obsidian armour and they know just how deadly it can be. Any combatant needs to break through its armour while avoiding its mace-like tail before standing a chance of damaging it.<br><br><col=F5B241>Quest</col>: TokTz-Ket-Dill<br><br><col=F5B241>Combat</col>: TokTz-Ket-Dill is immune to ranged and magic and, before you start dealing any damage, you'll want to mine through its thick armour (pickaxe provided in arena). Once broken, the TokTz-Ket-Dill is weak to crushing weapons. The beast will attack with melee and occasionally stomp the ground to rain rocks on your head.
param=dom_boss_1_taunt,Grrrr
param=dom_boss_taunt_sound_english,armadillo_roar
param=dom_boss_taunt_sound_german,armadillo_roar
param=dom_boss_taunt_sound_french,armadillo_roar
param=dom_boss_taunt_sound_portuguese,armadillo_roar
param=dom_battle_total_lifepoints,15000
param=dom_boss_spline_size,0
param=dom_boss_thumbnail,aif_dom_toktz

// 2791
[dom_boss_black_grey_white_golems]
param=dom_boss_name,Black, Grey and White Golems
param=dom_boss_id,36
param=dom_boss_npc_safe_1,dom_golem_black_safe
param=dom_boss_npc_safe_2,dom_golem_white_safe
param=dom_boss_npc_safe_3,dom_golem_grey_safe
param=dom_boss_npc_combat_1,dom_golem_black_combat
param=dom_boss_npc_combat_2,dom_golem_white_combat
param=dom_boss_npc_combat_3,dom_golem_grey_combat
param=dom_npc_spawn_npc1_x,39
param=dom_npc_spawn_npc1_z,33
param=dom_npc_spawn_npc2_x,38
param=dom_npc_spawn_npc2_z,32
param=dom_npc_spawn_npc3_x,39
param=dom_npc_spawn_npc3_z,31
param=dom_arena_type,2
param=dom_boss_desc,These creations are next to mindless. Following the instructions of their creators they will attack anything that comes near them unquestioningly. Their distinct colours are the only clues to their inner workings.<br><br><col=F5B241>Quest</col>: Spirits of the Elid<br><br><col=F5B241>Combat</col>: For all three golems, magic and ranged attacks are dramatically reduced. For the black golem you're best using crushing attacks; for the white golem you're best using stabbing attacks and for the grey golem you should use slashing attacks.
param=dom_boss_1_taunt,Destroy human
param=dom_boss_2_taunt,As my master wills it
param=dom_boss_3_taunt,Death to you
param=dom_boss_taunt_sound_english,golems_taunt
param=dom_boss_taunt_sound_german,golems_taunt
param=dom_boss_taunt_sound_french,golems_taunt
param=dom_boss_taunt_sound_portuguese,golems_taunt
param=dom_battle_total_lifepoints,16500
param=dom_boss_spline_size,0
param=dom_boss_thumbnail,aif_dom_bwg_golems

// 2792
[dom_boss_teus_dayth]
param=dom_boss_name,Treus Dayth
param=dom_boss_id,37
param=dom_boss_npc_safe_1,dom_treus_dayth_safe
param=dom_boss_npc_safe_2,dom_possessed_pickaxe_safe
param=dom_boss_npc_safe_3,dom_possessed_pickaxe_safe
param=dom_boss_npc_safe_4,dom_possessed_pickaxe_safe
param=dom_boss_npc_combat_1,dom_treus_dayth_combat
param=dom_boss_npc_combat_2,dom_possessed_pickaxe_combat
param=dom_boss_npc_combat_3,dom_possessed_pickaxe_combat
param=dom_boss_npc_combat_4,dom_possessed_pickaxe_combat
param=dom_npc_spawn_npc1_x,38
param=dom_npc_spawn_npc1_z,31
param=dom_npc_spawn_npc2_x,39
param=dom_npc_spawn_npc2_z,33
param=dom_npc_spawn_npc3_x,40
param=dom_npc_spawn_npc3_z,31
param=dom_npc_spawn_npc4_x,39
param=dom_npc_spawn_npc4_z,29
param=dom_arena_type,2
param=dom_boss_desc,Treus is the guardian of the dangerous crystals in the haunted mine below the river Salve, or at least he was until he died - and now it's his spirit that lingers on. This supernatural being has the ability to possess and control objects around him. Luckily in this tower it's 'only' pickaxes any combatant has to worry about.<br><br><col=F5B241>Quest</col>: Haunted Mine<br><br><col=F5B241>Combat</col>: The more damaged Treus is the more likely he is to show his cowardly nature and run from you, fading and teleporting away. Hit him to turn him back into his true form. He attacks (when he's not running away) with melee. He is also accompanied by three possessed pickaxes.
param=dom_boss_1_taunt,Your death is imminent
param=dom_boss_2_taunt,
param=dom_boss_3_taunt,
param=dom_boss_4_taunt,
param=dom_boss_taunt_sound_english,silence
param=dom_boss_taunt_sound_german,silence
param=dom_boss_taunt_sound_french,silence
param=dom_boss_taunt_sound_portuguese,silence
param=dom_battle_total_lifepoints,4500
param=dom_boss_spline_size,0
param=dom_boss_thumbnail,aif_dom_treus_dayth

// 2793
[dom_boss_elvarg]
param=dom_boss_name,Elvarg
param=dom_boss_id,38
param=dom_boss_npc_safe_1,dom_elvarg_safe
param=dom_boss_npc_combat_1,dom_elvarg_combat
param=dom_npc_spawn_npc1_x,36
param=dom_npc_spawn_npc1_z,30
param=dom_arena_type,1
param=dom_boss_desc,The giant green dragon of Crandor, Elvarg was awoken on the island by an adventurer and anyone nearby soon suffered her wrath. One person she didn't kill was Melzar. A pretty unforgettable chap.<br><br><col=F5B241>Quest</col>: Dragon Slayer<br><br><col=F5B241>Combat</col>: Possibly one of the most famous dragons to ever live, Elvarg attacks with a mixture of melee and dragon fire breath. You better have a anti-dragonbreath shield with you if you want to limit the damage you receive.
param=dom_boss_1_taunt,Roaar
param=dom_boss_taunt_sound_english,dragon_ready_yawn_1
param=dom_boss_taunt_sound_german,dragon_ready_yawn_1
param=dom_boss_taunt_sound_french,dragon_ready_yawn_1
param=dom_boss_taunt_sound_portuguese,dragon_ready_yawn_1
param=dom_battle_total_lifepoints,9000
param=dom_boss_spline_size,0
param=dom_boss_thumbnail,aif_dom_elvarg

// 2794
[dom_boss_culinaromancer]
param=dom_boss_name,Culinaromancer
param=dom_boss_id,39
param=dom_boss_npc_safe_1,dom_culinaromancer_safe
param=dom_boss_npc_combat_1,dom_culinaromancer_combat
param=dom_npc_spawn_npc1_x,38
param=dom_npc_spawn_npc1_z,32
param=dom_arena_type,3
param=dom_boss_desc,A lunatic chef that was once renowned for his culinary creations in Lumbridge Castle. His insane drive for domination soon came to light and he was imprisoned. Having broken free, he needs to be stopped before he carves someone up with that vicious looking meat cleaver he carries.<br><br><col=F5B241>Quest</col>: Recipe for Disaster<br><br><col=F5B241>Combat</col>: This twisted chef will attack with magic. Not so strong without his minions to protect him now!
param=dom_boss_1_taunt,No more meals for you, fool
param=dom_boss_taunt_sound_english,culinaromancer_no_more_meals
param=dom_boss_taunt_sound_german,culinaromancer_no_more_meals
