[early_bird_tzhaar2_minigame_must_collect]
param=early_bird_description,For reaching wave 30 of the Fight Kiln during the Early Bird period, you are awarded with a...
param=early_bird_bonus_1,70K XP lamp for any skill
param=early_bird_more_info,You must collect this XP lamp from TokHaar-Hok in the Fight Kiln.

// 7333
[early_bird_tzhaar2_minigame]
param=early_bird_description,For reaching wave 30 of the Fight Kiln during the Early Bird period, you are awarded with a...
param=early_bird_bonus_1,70K XP lamp for any skill
param=early_bird_more_info,You can claim the XP by rubbing the Early Bird lamp in your inventory.

// 7334
[early_bird_tzhaar2_quest]
param=early_bird_description,For completing The Elder Kiln during the Early Bird period, you are awarded with an XP tome that grants...
param=early_bird_bonus_1,50K Magic XP
param=early_bird_bonus_2,30K Agility XP
param=early_bird_bonus_3,100K combat XP
param=early_bird_more_info,You can claim the XP by reading the Early Bird tome in your inventory.

// 7335
[dom_boss_special_it_burns]
param=dom_boss_name,Special: The Fire! It Burns!
param=dom_boss_npc_safe_1,dom_stunfeer_safe
param=dom_boss_npc_combat_1,dom_stunfeer_ground_combat
param=dom_npc_spawn_npc1_x,41
param=dom_npc_spawn_npc1_z,30
param=dom_arena_type,1
param=dom_boss_desc,<br><br><br><br><br><br><br><br><br><br>An incalculable number of creatures have been summoned from memories in the tower. As it turns out, creatures aren't exclusively drawn from memories: the fears, combat expertise and dark desires of warriors have seeped into the tower, until one horrific day when a creature was born: the Sunfreet.<br><br><col=F5B241>Combat</col>: The Sunfreet switches between two states: one in the air and one on the ground. While in the air, you'll want to be careful of its fierce fire-breathing, and it'll take you time to learn the pattern of its attack. While on the ground, it's at your disposal, although it fiercely attacks with its spear-like tail and flaming breath.<br><br>If you should see it inhale, be prepared to turn the other way, unless you wish to be stunned. The Sunfreet will also make a sweeping attack with its tail, for which retreat is the only sensible option. Get it close to death and you'll find it altogether more aggressive. Dragonfire shields won't help protect you.<br><br>You will also have the following handicaps applied: no power-ups, no familiars, no ultimate abilities, no prayers.<br><br><col=F5B241>A character is born</col>: The visual design of the Sunfreet was chosen by attendants of RuneFest 2011, a celebration of all things RuneScape. Based on the concept art and model created at the festival in London, we designed the mechanics to match. Anyone paying close attention might have noticed that the name of the beast is an anagram of 'RuneFest'. Thank you to all the warriors who voted on the design, as it was your 'fears, combat expertise and dark desires' that brought him to life!<br><br><col=F5B241>Quests required to play</col>: None.
param=dom_boss_1_taunt,
param=dom_boss_taunt_sound_english,stunfeer_roar
param=dom_boss_taunt_sound_german,stunfeer_roar
param=dom_boss_taunt_sound_french,stunfeer_roar
param=dom_boss_taunt_sound_portuguese,stunfeer_roar
param=dom_battle_total_lifepoints,60000
param=dom_boss_spline_size,3

// 7336
[dom_boss_special_it_burns_easy]
param=dom_boss_name,Special: The Fire! It Burns! (easy version)
param=dom_boss_npc_safe_1,dom_stunfeer_safe_easy
param=dom_boss_npc_combat_1,dom_stunfeer_ground_combat_easy
param=dom_npc_spawn_npc1_x,41
param=dom_npc_spawn_npc1_z,30
param=dom_arena_type,1
param=dom_boss_desc,<br><br><br><br><br><br><br><br><br><br>An incalculable number of creatures have been summoned from memories in the tower. As it turns out, creatures aren't exclusively drawn from memories: the fears, combat expertise and dark desires of warriors have seeped into the tower, until one horrific day when a creature was born: the Sunfreet.<br><br><col=F5B241>Combat</col>: This version of the Sunfreet is a lot easier than the standard version. The Sunfreet switches between two states: one in the air and one on the ground. While in the air, you'll want to be careful of its fierce fire-breathing, and it'll take you time to learn the pattern of its attack. While on the ground, it's at your disposal, although it fiercely attacks with its spear-like tail and flaming breath.<br><br>If you should see it inhale, be prepared to turn the other way, unless you wish to be stunned. The Sunfreet will also make a sweeping attack with its tail, for which retreat is the only sensible option. Get it close to death and you'll find it altogether more aggressive. Dragonfire shields won't help protect you.<br><br>You will also have the following handicaps applied: no power-ups, no familiars, no ultimate abilities, no prayers.<br><br><col=F5B241>A character is born</col>: The visual design of the Sunfreet was chosen by attendants of RuneFest 2011, a celebration of all things RuneScape. Based on the concept art and model created at the festival in London, we designed the mechanics to match. Anyone paying close attention might have noticed that the name of the beast is an anagram of 'RuneFest'. Thank you to all the warriors who voted on the design, as it was your 'fears, combat expertise and dark desires' that brought him to life!<br><br><col=F5B241>Quests required to play</col>: None.
param=dom_boss_1_taunt,
param=dom_boss_taunt_sound_english,stunfeer_roar
param=dom_boss_taunt_sound_german,stunfeer_roar
param=dom_boss_taunt_sound_french,stunfeer_roar
param=dom_boss_taunt_sound_portuguese,stunfeer_roar
param=dom_battle_total_lifepoints,10000
param=dom_boss_spline_size,3

