param=bslay_tactic_title,Grasping Hands
param=bslay_tactic_text,The Black Stone Crystals on Seiryu's back emit a trail of grasping shadowy hands that move across the arena and deal significant damage.

// 26536
[bslay_dungeon_aminishi3_enigmas]
param=bslay_tactic_title,Shadow Enigmas
param=bslay_tactic_text,Once Seiryu is incapacitated, the crystals open a portal from which a large hand made of black stone appears. Formless shadowy blobs called Shadow Enigmas pour out from the portal and are immediately drawn to Seiryu's head. If they reach Seiryu, they <col=FFFFFF>heal</col> the Black Stone Crystals for a great deal of lifepoints.
param=bslay_tactic_new_npc,dungeon_aminishi_boss3_corruption

// 26537
[bslay_dungeon_dragonfort1_damage]
param=bslay_tactic_title,Phase Shift
param=bslay_tactic_text,Powerful celestial dragons can phase through dimensional space, and thus Astellarn takes greatly reduced damage as she is able to mitigate direct hits. Standing in a stabilised <col=FFFFFF>Wyrmhole</col> will balance out this effect however.

// 26538
[bslay_dungeon_dragonfort1_rain]
param=bslay_tactic_title,Celestial Rain
param=bslay_tactic_text,Cosmic rain particles will fall on random quadrants in the arena, causing increased <col=FFFFFF>typeless</col> damage over time.

// 26539
[bslay_egwd_bik_boss_dead_beast]
param=bslay_tactic_title,Dead Beasts
param=bslay_tactic_text,In each corner of the graveyard are long-dead, preserved beasts. After the disruption caused from Croesus, these buried creatures have been uncovered and are a perfect resource for Croesus's fungus to grow. Remove the fungus from these to weaken Croesus and gather useful resources. Be vigilant - removed fungus will eventually grow back and strengthen Croesus again. Use rotten fungus to create a poisonous paste that can slow down the regrowth.

