// 30560
[bslay_arraxi_tactics_p1]
param=bslay_tactic_title,Stage One
param=bslay_tactic_text,When the Araxxi encounter begins, you'll be contained within a starting area.<br>To progress you must pick one of the two burnable webs to set fire to. After a minute the web will burn away and you can progress to stage two. The webs you can burn change every four days.<br><br>In this stage Araxxor can <col=FFFFFF>Cocoon, Cleave</col> and <col=FFFFFF>Web Shield.</col><br><br>There are three types of styles that Araxxor can spawn in, <col=FFFFFF>Ranged</col> represented by <col=FFFFFF>green legs</col>, and will apply a poison dot throughout the fight, <col=FFFFFF>Magic</col> represented by <col=FFFFFF>blue legs</col>, and damage throughout the fight will slowly drain stats and lower overload timers and <col=FFFFFF>Melee</col> represented by <col=FFFFFF>red legs</col>, and will apply a damage over time effect that increases randomly throughout the effect's lifetime.

// 30561
[bslay_arraxi_tactics_p1_cocoon]
param=bslay_tactic_title,Cocoon
param=bslay_tactic_text,When fired, you will become encased in webbing. The more you click the more you will break free. Using the ability <col=E6DCB4>Freedom</col> or <col=E6DCB4>Anticipation</col> before this attack will help lower the amount you are cocooned for.
param=bslay_tactic_animation,sb_spider_boss_01_cocoon_attack
param=bslay_tactic_spotanim,sb_spider_boss_01_cocoon_attack_spotanim
param=bslay_tactic_spotanim_model,sb_spider_boss_01_cocoon_attack_spotanim

// 30562
[bslay_arraxi_tactics_p1_webshield]
param=bslay_tactic_title,Web Shield
param=bslay_tactic_text,A web shielding will cover the boss for 10 seconds. While this is present, the boss will take half damage and reflect half damage to you. If you don't attack, the boss will heal while the shield is present.
param=bslay_tactic_animation,sb_spider_boss_01_web_shield
param=bslay_tactic_spotanim,sb_spider_boss_01_web_shield_spotanim
param=bslay_tactic_spotanim_model,sb_spider_boss_01_web_shield_spotanim

// 30563
[bslay_arraxi_tactics_p1_cleave]
param=bslay_tactic_title,Cleave
param=bslay_tactic_text,The boss will pull you towards them if you haven't used the <col=E6DCB4>Freedom</col> or <col=E6DCB4>Anticipation</col> ability. Cleave will hit massive damage to anyone caught in front of the boss.
param=bslay_tactic_animation,sb_spider_boss_01_cleave_attack
param=bslay_tactic_spotanim,sb_spider_boss_01_cleave_attack_spotanim
param=bslay_tactic_spotanim_model,sb_spider_boss_01_cleave_attack_spotanim

// 30564
[bslay_arraxi_tactics_p2]
param=bslay_tactic_title,Stage Two
param=bslay_tactic_text,After the web has burned away, you can venture down your chosen path. Depending on what path you choose, Araxxor will gain new attacks. You'll have to deal with these before progressing to Stage Three.

// 30565
[bslay_arraxi_tactics_p2_burn_spawn]
param=bslay_tactic_title,Burn spawn
param=bslay_tactic_text,In all paths, Araxxor will spawn a few eggs which will hatch into aggressive spiders if not dealt with. Luckily he'll also launch a fiery projectile towards you. If this explodes on the eggs it will destroy them - enraging the boss!
param=bslay_tactic_animation,sb_spider_boss_01_burn_bomb
param=bslay_tactic_spotanim,sb_spider_boss_01_burn_bomb_spotanim
param=bslay_tactic_spotanim_model,sb_spider_boss_01_burn_bomb_spotanim

// 30566
[bslay_arraxi_tactics_p2_adds]
param=bslay_tactic_title,Path One: More Spiders!
param=bslay_tactic_text,If you take the top path, Araxxor will try and spawn spiders to help kill you. Other than standard spiders, he can spawn a <col=FFFFFF>pulsing spider</col> that will heal him while it lives, and a <col=FFFFFF>mirrorback spider</col> that will make the boss reflect all damage while the mirrorback is alive.

// 30567
[bslay_arraxi_tactics_p2_acid_spiders]
param=bslay_tactic_title,Path Two: Acid Spiders
param=bslay_tactic_text,If you take the middle path, Araxxor can fire a projectile at the floor leaving an acidic puddle on the floor for ten seconds. <br><br>After this time the puddle will form into an acidic spider that will rush towards you, exploding for massive damage after a short amount of time or if it touches you.
param=bslay_tactic_animation,sb_spider_boss_01_melee_attack

// 30568
[bslay_arraxi_tactics_p2_acid_ramp]
param=bslay_tactic_title,Acidic Ramp
param=bslay_tactic_text,On path two you must degrade the ramp to progress to Stage Three. To do this you must have Araxxor stay in the acid pool to absorb the acid.<br><br>You need him to have at least half the acid to degrade the ramp - note that it will drip off him if he isn't in the pool.

// 30569
[bslay_arraxi_tactics_p2_darkness]
param=bslay_tactic_title,Darkness
param=bslay_tactic_text,If you take path three, Araxxor will plunge the entire area into darkness which will inflict increasing damage over time if you do not stand in the light beams.

// 30570
[bslay_arraxi_tactics_p2_qte]
param=bslay_tactic_title,Charge
param=bslay_tactic_text,Roughly every minute in path three, Araxxor will drop down from the ceiling and charge you. If you make an attempt to dodge he'll smash into the wall behind.<br><br>Dodging in the correct direction prevents you from taking damage and causes the most damage to the wall, with only two being required for the wall to cave in.
param=bslay_tactic_animation,sb_spider_boss_01_attack_low

// 30571
[bslay_arraxi_tactics_p3_finish_mechanics]
param=bslay_tactic_title,Stage three: Finish him!
param=bslay_tactic_text,On entry to stage three, Araxxor will prioritise finishing off any path mechanics you didn't finish. He may spawn acid spiders if you chose path two and spiders if you chose path one.<br><br>On top of this, the path you didn't pick will become active, so those attacks will occur in stage 3 until Araxxor dies.

// 30572
[bslay_arraxi_tactics_p4_araxxi]
param=bslay_tactic_title,Stage four: Araxxi
param=bslay_tactic_text,After you have defeated Araxxor, Araxxi will consume him. Araxxi will use any left over attacks (such as acid or spider minions) as well as performing <col=FFFFFF>Cleave, Web Shield</col> and <col=FFFFFF>Cocoon</col>.<br><br>As Araxxi drops below 50% health she will stop doing special attacks and instead grow increasingly damaging.<br><br>As Araxxi goes below 25% health (or 35% in duo), she will enrage faster and spawn an acid wave that tracks the target down until they are hit. When the acid wave hits, it will remain on the target until they move away, at which point it will bounce away and start again.
param=bslay_tactic_animation,sb_spider_boss_01_magic_attack
param=bslay_tactic_spotanim,sb_spider_boss_01_magic_attack_spotanim
param=bslay_tactic_spotanim_model,sb_spider_boss_01_magic_attack_spotanim

// 30573
[bslay_barrows_tactics_intro]
param=bslay_tactic_title,The Crypts
param=bslay_tactic_text,In the Barrows, there are six barrow mounds. Each leads to a crypt which contains one of the infamous Barrows Brothers. One of the brothers won't be present and instead his grave will give access to the area beneath the crypts.<br><br>In the area beneath the crypts you'll have a chance to encounter any brothers you've not killed. Navigating to the centre will grant access to the reward chest.<br>The more Barrows Brothers you kill, the better chance you'll have to receive loot!

// 30574
[bslay_barrows_tactics_ahrim]
param=bslay_tactic_title,Ahrim the Blighted
param=bslay_tactic_text,Ahrim is a mage of great strength and will attack with powerful fire spells.<br>There is a 1/4 chance with every attack that Ahrim will drain your Strength level.
param=bslay_tactic_animation,human_castcurse_staff
param=bslay_tactic_spotanim,curse_casting
param=bslay_tactic_spotanim_model,spells_curse_casting
param=bslay_tactic_new_npc,barrows_ahrim

// 30575
[bslay_barrows_tactics_dharok]
param=bslay_tactic_title,Dharok the Wretched
param=bslay_tactic_text,Dharok wields a massive greataxe. As he attacks you, he'll hit harder the lower his life points are. Protecting for melee or staying at a distance is recommended.
param=bslay_tactic_animation,barrow_dharok_crush
param=bslay_tactic_new_npc,barrows_dharok

// 30576
[bslay_barrows_tactics_guthan]
param=bslay_tactic_title,Guthan the Infested
param=bslay_tactic_text,Guthan uses his warspear to sap health from his victims. With every attack there is a 1/4 chance he'll heal what he hits!
param=bslay_tactic_animation,barrows_war_spear_stab
param=bslay_tactic_new_npc,barrows_guthan

// 30577
[bslay_barrows_tactics_karil]
param=bslay_tactic_title,Karil the Tainted
param=bslay_tactic_text,Karil is a strong ranger and uses his repeating crossbow to deal damage. There is a 1/4 chance he'll drain your Magic level if he hits you.
param=bslay_tactic_animation,barrows_repeating_crossbow_fire
param=bslay_tactic_new_npc,barrows_karil

// 30578
[bslay_barrows_tactics_torag]
param=bslay_tactic_title,Torag the Corrupted
param=bslay_tactic_text,Torag uses his massive hammer to smash his foes. There is a 1/4 chance his melee attacks will drain 5% of your Adrenaline.
param=bslay_tactic_animation,barrow_torag_crush
param=bslay_tactic_new_npc,barrows_torag

// 30579
[bslay_barrows_tactics_verac]
param=bslay_tactic_title,Verac the Defiled
param=bslay_tactic_text,Verac wears unholy armour that grants his warmace a 1/4 chance to ignore his opponent's armour!
param=bslay_tactic_animation,barrow_guthan_crush
param=bslay_tactic_new_npc,barrows_verac

// 30580
[bslay_barrows_tactics_akrisae]
param=bslay_tactic_title,Akrisae the Doomed
param=bslay_tactic_text,Akrisae the Doomed is located north in Verac's tomb. Those who fight him should be prepared - he can pray against your attacks and switch styles in reaction to your attacks.
param=bslay_tactic_animation,barrow_torag_crush
param=bslay_tactic_new_npc,mah5_barrows_akrisae

// 30581
[bslay_rots_tactics_intro]
param=bslay_tactic_title,The Shadow Realm
param=bslay_tactic_text,At the start of the encounter, the shadow binds the brothers together. If a brother is defeated, you must defeat another within 30 seconds or the shadow will revive all brothers to fight once more. Defeating a brother will also reset the revive timers of other brothers, and it will heal any brother still standing.<br><br>At the start of the fight one brother will be more in contact with the Shadow Realm and there is a chance he will send all players to the Shadow Realm at a point in the fight.<br><br>Inside the Shadow Realm, all special attacks the brothers perform will have increased accuracy and damage.<br>Be warned! If no-one is present on one side of the encounter, the shadow will send all brothers to the other side, when they are all back up.

// 30582
[bslay_rots_tactics_ahrim]
param=bslay_tactic_title,Ahrim
param=bslay_tactic_text,Ahrim will use standard fire attacks against his opponent that have a 1/8 chance to drain Strength levels. He also uses the <col=FFFFFF>Flight, Telejump, Shadow Pits</col>, and <col=FFFFFF>Turret of Fire</col> special attacks.

// 30583
[bslay_rots_tactics_ahrim_flight]
param=bslay_tactic_title,Ahrim: Flight
param=bslay_tactic_text,When Ahrim drops below 90% life points, he'll take the air. When flying, Ahrim will only use standard attacks against you. While flying Ahrim is immune to melee damage and takes 50% magic damage.

// 30584
[bslay_rots_tactics_ahrim_telejump]
param=bslay_tactic_title,Ahrim: Telejump
param=bslay_tactic_text,Ahrim will Telejump to a pillar in the centre of the arena and begin attacking the other side of the encounter - as well as lighting all the shadow pits on the other side.
param=bslay_tactic_new_npc,barrows2_ahrim
param=bslay_tactic_animation,barrows_brothers_smoke_tele_out
param=bslay_tactic_spotanim,rand_boss_demon_ghan_ko_magic_impact
param=bslay_tactic_spotanim_model,rand_demon_ghan_ko_magic_impact

// 30585
[bslay_rots_tactics_ahrim_firepits]
param=bslay_tactic_title,Ahrim: Shadow Pits
param=bslay_tactic_text,When Ahrim sets a pit to shadow, it'll glow brightly and hurt anyone caught in it. There is a 1/8 chance Ahrim's pit will be red. Any brother that walks in a red shadow pit will heal.

// 30586
[bslay_rots_tactics_ahrim_turretoffire]
param=bslay_tactic_title,Ahrim: Turret of Fire
param=bslay_tactic_text,Ahrim will teleport to a spot in the room and ignite his hands. As he rotates on the spot, anyone caught in the flames will take heavy fire damage.<br>
param=bslay_tactic_new_npc,barrows2_ahrim
param=bslay_tactic_animation,barrows2_brothers_turret_of_doom_loop
param=bslay_tactic_spotanim,barrows2_brothers_turret_of_doom_spotanim
param=bslay_tactic_spotanim_model,barrows2_brothers_turret_of_doom_fire_spotanim

// 30587
[bslay_rots_tactics_dharok]
param=bslay_tactic_title,Dharok
param=bslay_tactic_text,Dharok uses damaging melee attacks that get far stronger the fewer life points he has.<br><br>Dharok can use the <col=FFFFFF>Greatest Axe, Wall Slam,</col> and <col=FFFFFF>Hurricane</col> special attacks.

// 30588
[bslay_rots_tactics_dharok_greatestaxe]
param=bslay_tactic_title,Dharok: Greatest Axe
param=bslay_tactic_text,Dharok raises his greataxe for <col=FFFFFF>10</col> seconds, storing any damage in it that is done against him. After the 10 seconds, he'll unleash it on his next attack!
param=bslay_tactic_new_npc,barrows2_dharok
param=bslay_tactic_animation,barrows2_dharok_greatest_axe
param=bslay_tactic_spotanim,game_barrows2_dharok_greatest_axe_spotanim
param=bslay_tactic_spotanim_model,barrows2_dharok_greatest_axe_spotanim

// 30589
[bslay_rots_tactics_dharok_wallslam]
param=bslay_tactic_title,Dharok: Wall Slam
param=bslay_tactic_text,Dharok runs to a nearby wall, runs up it and then flings himself towards his original target, slamming down for massive damage.
param=bslay_tactic_new_npc,barrows2_dharok
param=bslay_tactic_animation,barrows2_brother_wall_run

// 30590
[bslay_rots_tactics_dharok_hurricane]
param=bslay_tactic_title,Dharok: Hurricane
param=bslay_tactic_text,Dharok starts spinning wildly towards his opponent, hitting all nearby with his greataxe for heavy damage.<br>
param=bslay_tactic_new_npc,barrows2_dharok
param=bslay_tactic_animation,barrows2_brother_hurricane_spin
param=bslay_tactic_spotanim,game_barrows2_brothers_hurricane_spotanim
param=bslay_tactic_spotanim_model,combat_2012_sword_trail_spotanim

// 30591
[bslay_rots_tactics_guthan]
param=bslay_tactic_title,Guthan
param=bslay_tactic_text,Guthan uses his warspear, which has a 1/8 chance to heal an amount equal to his hit.<br><br>Guthan can use the <col=FFFFFF>Impale, Hurricane,</col> and <col=FFFFFF>Throw</col> special attacks.

// 30592
[bslay_rots_tactics_guthan_impale]
param=bslay_tactic_title,Guthan: Impale
param=bslay_tactic_text,Guthan will try to throw his spear at a player he isn't targetting. If the spear impales the target they will bleed for heavy damage, until they run to Guthan and he pulls it back out of them.
param=bslay_tactic_new_npc,barrows2_guthan
param=bslay_tactic_animation,barrows2_guthan_throwspear

// 30593
[bslay_rots_tactics_guthan_hurricane]
param=bslay_tactic_title,Guthan: Hurricane
param=bslay_tactic_text,Guthan starts spinning wildly towards his opponent, hitting all nearby with his warspear for heavy damage.
param=bslay_tactic_new_npc,barrows2_guthan
param=bslay_tactic_animation,barrows2_brother_hurricane_spin
param=bslay_tactic_spotanim,game_barrows2_brothers_hurricane_spotanim
param=bslay_tactic_spotanim_model,combat_2012_sword_trail_spotanim

// 30594
[bslay_rots_tactics_guthan_throw]
param=bslay_tactic_title,Guthan: Throw
param=bslay_tactic_text,Guthan will try to locate Ahrim, Karil, or Verac to throw them. If successful, he'll <col=E6DCB4>Surge</col> over to them and throw them to a random nearby location, inflicting damage to anyone near where they land.<br>
param=bslay_tactic_new_npc,barrows2_guthan
param=bslay_tactic_animation,barrows2_throw

// 30595
[bslay_rots_tactics_karil]
param=bslay_tactic_title,Karil
param=bslay_tactic_text,Karil uses his twin pistol crossbows to inflict ranged damage. There is a 1/8 chance his attacks will drain Attack and Magic levels.<br><br>Karil can also use the <col=FFFFFF>Portal Dash, Lightning Conductor</col> and <col=FFFFFF>Bombard</col> special attacks.

// 30596
[bslay_rots_tactics_karil_portaldash]
param=bslay_tactic_title,Karil: Portal Dash
param=bslay_tactic_text,Karil will summon a shadow portal at his location that he uses to dash to the other side of the encounter.<br><br>He will continue jumping side-to-side until he runs out of portals. After <col=FFFFFF>4 seconds</col> the shadow portal will explode, dealing massive damage to those nearby, less if they are further away.<br><br>If you enter a shadow portal you will close it, preventing it from exploding but taking more damage if you have been through portals before.
param=bslay_tactic_new_npc,barrows2_karil
param=bslay_tactic_animation,barrows_brothers_smoke_tele_out
param=bslay_tactic_spotanim,barrows2_brothers_smoke_tele_out_spotanim
param=bslay_tactic_spotanim_model,barrows2_brothers_smoke_tele_in_spotanim

// 30597
[bslay_rots_tactics_karil_lightning]
param=bslay_tactic_title,Karil: Lightning Conductor
param=bslay_tactic_text,Karil will teleport to a spot in the room and unleash shadow-lightning from his hands. As he rotates on the spot, anyone caught in the lightning will take heavy damage.
param=bslay_tactic_new_npc,barrows2_karil
param=bslay_tactic_animation,barrows2_brothers_turret_of_doom_loop
param=bslay_tactic_spotanim,barrows2_brothers_turret_of_doom_spotanim
param=bslay_tactic_spotanim_model,barrows2_brothers_turret_of_doom_electric_spotanim

// 30598
[bslay_rots_tactics_karil_bombard]
param=bslay_tactic_title,Karil: Bombard
param=bslay_tactic_text,Karil will teleport to a pillar in the centre of the arena and begin attacking the other side of the encounter - as well as unleashing a massive lightning barrage down a strip of the room on the other side.<br>
param=bslay_tactic_new_npc,barrows2_karil
param=bslay_tactic_animation,combat_2012_auto_attack_melee_unarmed
param=bslay_tactic_spotanim,barrows2_karil_lightning_bolt_spotanim
param=bslay_tactic_spotanim_model,barrows2_karil_lightning_bolt_spotanim

// 30599
[bslay_rots_tactics_torag]
param=bslay_tactic_title,Torag
param=bslay_tactic_text,Torag uses his massive hammer to deal melee damage. He has a 1/8 chance to reduce his opponents' adrenaline by 5%, and can use the <col=FFFFFF>Hurricane, Throw, Wall Slam</col>, and <col=FFFFFF>Whack</col> special attacks.

// 30600
[bslay_rots_tactics_torag_hurricane]
